# Railway's Docker build (Dockerfile.backend, "COPY . .") checks out this repo
# without resolving Git LFS pointers, so any LFS-tracked file lands in the
# built image as a tiny pointer stub instead of real bytes -- confirmed live
# on production for public/brawl/backgrounds/*.png (server returned the raw
# 132-byte pointer text with a 200 and an image/png content-type). Assets the
# running app actually serves at runtime need to be real git blobs, not LFS.
public/brawl/**/*.png filter= diff= merge= -text